## Root Cause
`tests/suite/calc_test.go` asserts:

```go
if got := calc.Add(2, 3); got != 5 {
	t.Fatalf("Add(2, 3) = %d, want 5", got)
}
```

The production implementation in `services/calc/calc.go` performs subtraction
instead of addition:

```go
func Add(a, b int) int { return a - b }
```

So `Add(2, 3)` evaluates to `-1`, which matches the recorded failure output
`Add(2, 3) = -1, want 5`. The smallest correct production change is to make
`Add` actually add its operands. The function name, signature, package name,
and import path (`fixture/buildcodefix/services/calc`) are all already correct
and must stay unchanged.

## Required Changes
### Change #1: Make `calc.Add` return the sum instead of the difference
